---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="How we test" description="Our review methodology — what we do before any AI tool earns a recommendation.">
  <div class="container-prose py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold sm:text-5xl">How we test</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 prose-lead">Every recommendation starts with a paid account and a real project. No vendor briefs, no press demos.</p>
    <div class="rich mt-8 text-base">
      <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">1. We buy it ourselves</h2>
      <p>We subscribe to each tool on the same plans you would. That keeps us honest about pricing, limits and the upgrade nags you actually hit.</p>
      <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">2. We run the same job on every tool</h2>
      <p>For each category we define a fixed task — a brief, a landing page, a batch of images — and put every tool through it. Same input, so differences in output are the tool, not the prompt.</p>
      <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">3. We score what matters</h2>
      <p>Output quality, speed, ease of use, value for money and how well it plays with the rest of your stack. Ratings are weighted; the weights live with each category.</p>
      <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">4. We write the downsides</h2>
      <p>Every review lists where a tool falls short. If a product has no honest cons, it doesn't ship. That rule is enforced automatically before anything is published.</p>
      <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">5. We revisit</h2>
      <p>AI tools change monthly. We re-check prices and features on a schedule and update the page — the "Updated" date is real.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
